1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,310
Alex: The Catholic Church rejects blaming all Jews for Jesus’s death.

2
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:14,590
Maya: There’s an official document: Nostra aetate, issued in nineteen-sixty-five. Its fourth section directly addresses that collective accusation, instead of leaving it to rumor.

3
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:24,540
Alex: It says Jesus’s suffering cannot be charged indiscriminately to all Jewish people alive then, or to Jewish people today. It also condemns antisemitism.

4
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:34,320
Maya: That doesn’t erase the harm the accusation caused. And one declaration didn’t make prejudice disappear. But it matters when someone presents collective blame as Catholic teaching.

5
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:45,700
Alex: You can discuss religious texts and disagree about theology. That is different from making people guilty because they belong to a community, especially generations later.

6
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:52,300
Maya: So check what the document actually says, not a comment claiming to speak for an entire faith.

7
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:58,220
Alex: You don’t inherit guilt from a stranger’s history.

